    "\n",
    "Normalize Unicode, preserve French accents, separate punctuation and keep sentences up to eight English tokens and ten French tokens. Retain one French reference per normalized English sentence, then select 6,000 distinct source sentences: up to 1,000 shopping-related examples and a random selection of the remaining short sentences. This is a documented educational subset, rather than a claim to have trained on the entire corpus.\n",
    "\n",
    "Split by distinct normalized English source into 80% training, 10% validation and 10% test. Fit vocabularies only on training data. The test data is not used for fitting tokenizers, updating model weights or selecting the best epoch."
