   "source": [
    "### Tokenization and teacher forcing\n",
    "\n",
    "The project uses an encoder–decoder with attention so the decoder can consult individual source states. This extends the fixed repeated context shown in the introductory example. Add `startseq` and `endseq` to French sentences. During training, the decoder receives the preceding correct French tokens and predicts the next tokens; this is teacher forcing. During inference it receives its own previous prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "Padding is excluded from the project loss and token accuracy. Each sentence contributes equally to the reported average of its non-padding token losses and accuracies. Source attention also masks padding. Unknown words receive an explicit `[unk]` token. The maximum vocabulary is 2,500 tokens per language, including reserved tokens."
   ]
  },
